%% Diagram: EventBridge Archive & Replay - Sequence Flow
%% Source lecture: AWS EventBridge Crash Course - Lecture: "Archives & Replay"
%% Description:  Sequence diagram showing how events flow from a source to the
%%               default event bus, are continuously captured by an Archive,
%%               and later replayed by an Operator over a time range into a
%%               new target (e.g., a Lambda function for reprocessing).
%% Author: Prem Vishnoi <prem.vishnoi@example.com>
```mermaid
sequenceDiagram
    participant SRC as Event Source
    participant BUS as Default Event Bus
    participant ARCH as EventBridge Archive
    participant OP as Operator
    participant REPLAY as Replay
    participant TGT as Target<br/>Lambda

    Note over BUS,ARCH: All matching events are continuously archived
    SRC->>BUS: 1. Publish event (Order Placed)
    BUS-->>ARCH: 2. Archive ingests event

    Note over OP,REPLAY: Later, operator initiates a replay
    OP->>REPLAY: 3. StartReplay(start=09:00, end=10:00)
    REPLAY->>TGT: 4. Re-deliver archived events
    TGT-->>REPLAY: ack
    REPLAY-->>OP: Replay complete
```
